⟦ 20260817_s2_instrument_census_bidirectional | LEARNING-RECORD | vsm-1.2.1 | 2026-08-17T16:56:01Z ⟧

@vsm 1.2.1
@status(V) production
// LEARNING-RECORD §6 — S2 instrument census must be BIDIRECTIONAL.
// Class-level problem found by S3* audit of instrument uniqueness/conformance:
// a coordination map (agent_map.vsm) that covers only ONE layer of instruments
// (plugins TS) silently hides the rest (scripts, checks, engines) from S2.
// The system believes it has full S2 when the census is partial.

learning_record("20260817_s2_instrument_census_bidirectional") {
  uuid:      "b7a3f9c2-8d41-4e6a-b0c3-1f2a9d8e7c65",
  parent:    "20260817_daemon_gate_after_early_exit.vsm (audit trail)",
  family:    "instrumentation-census",
  class:     "verification-gap",
  severity:  "high",
  detection: "S3* audit 2026-08-17: agent_map.vsm declared 3 agents + 5
             plugins but 0 scripts, 0 checks, 0 core engines — the runtime
             inventory (opencode.json) had 5 plugins; the disk had 3 bash
             scripts + 44 checks + 22 vsl scripts. Censo parcial.",
  root_cause: "the map was built as a PLUGIN census (it answered 'which
             plugins does the boot load?'), not an INSTRUMENT census
             ('which organs operate and how do they avoid colliding?'). The
             first is a runtime question; the second is an S2 question.
             Nobody re-asked the question at the instrument layer.",
  fix:       "extended agent_map.vsm with instruments[] (role/substrate/
             event/reads-writes/design); agent-map-valid now censuses BOTH
             directions: map→reality (substrates exist) + reality→map
             (every plugin/script/engine declared, nothing invisible) +
             no-collision (no two writers on one substrate, A6).
             impl-with-design-valid gained 'map' mode: every instrument
             REGISTERED in the S2 map must self-declare design: (R16).
             relocate-vsm-valid gained 'selftest' mode: spec v1 done_when
             (round-trip, 0 broken) enforced by gate4.",
  verify:    "checks/agent-map-valid (pass/fail/collision discriminate),
             checks/impl-with-design-valid map (7 instruments all with
             design), checks/relocate-vsm-valid selftest (round-trip OK),
             full pre-commit green, boot-ontology 0 violations",
  lesson:    "A coordination map is only S2 if it covers the FULL instrument
             census — one layer covered is a hole, not a map. Uniqueness
             (A6) is not 'no two plugins exist' but 'no two instruments
             race on the same substrate' — and that contract must be
             DECLARED (reads/writes), never implicit. Every repair of this
             class is an AUTOMATIC instrument (check + gate), never a
             document edit.",
  organ:     "S3* (audit) → S2 (map) → R4.1 (checks) → pre-commit (gates)",
  recursion: "root system, agent layer",
  canonical: "docs/spec_revision/system/s5-policy/agent-policy/agent-map-v1/agent_map.vsm",
  evidence:  "checks/agent-map-valid: PASS censo bidireccional (EXIT=0);
             checks/impl-with-design-valid map: PASS 7 instruments (EXIT=0);
             checks/relocate-vsm-valid selftest: PASS round-trip (EXIT=0);
             pre-commit full: EXIT=0; boot-ontology: 0 violations",
  action:    "ALWAYS re-ask the census question at every new layer: if an
             organ exists (script, check, engine, service) it must be
             DECLARED in the S2 map with substrate + reads/writes + design.
             The map is the checklist — a registered instrument without
             design violates R16; an unregistered one violates S2.
             Run checks/agent-map-valid map + pass on every commit (wired
             in git_pre_commit.sh).",
  trace: {
    commit:   "5472a26e (fix(audit): instrument S2 full census)",
    gate_hit: "R4.1 (verify_claim.py agent-map-valid, impl-with-design-valid,
               relocate-vsm-valid); boot-load-test (verify_boot_primer hash
               drift — 8 plugin hashes re-baselined)",
  },
  propagation: "agent_map.vsm (agent-map-v1) + checks/agent-map-valid,
             impl-with-design-valid (modo map), relocate-vsm-valid
             (selftest), git_pre_commit.sh — todo instrumento
             (script/check/engine/servicio) debe declararse en el censo S2
             con substrate + reads/writes + design; un organ no declarado
             viola S2, uno sin design viola R16 (A6: dos writers sobre el
             mismo substrate).",
}
⟦ /20260817_s2_instrument_census_bidirectional ⟧
